========================================
ML + DFT PROJECT TRAINING INSTRUCTIONS
========================================

----------------------------------------
0. INITIAL SETUP CHECK
----------------------------------------

Ensure the following folder structure exists:

project_root/
│
├── data/raw/nebBVSE122k/
│ ├── nebBVSE122k_train.xyz
│ ├── nebBVSE122k_test.xyz
│
├── data/raw/nebDFT2k/
│ └── nebDFT2k_centroids.xyz
│
├── data/processed/
├── models/
├── results/

----------------------------------------
1. SANITY CHECK DATA
----------------------------------------

Run:

python inspect_data.py

Expected:
- No errors
- Prints number of structures
- Prints min, max, mean barrier
- Shows histogram

Check:
- No NaNs
- Barrier values reasonable (~0–3 eV)

----------------------------------------
2. PRECOMPUTE DFT GRAPHS
----------------------------------------

Run:

python precompute_dft.py

This:
- Reads DFT xyz file
- Converts structures → graph format
- Saves processed dataset

Output file created:

data/processed/dft_centroids.pt

----------------------------------------
3. SPLIT DFT DATASET
----------------------------------------

Run:

python DFT_Training/split_dft.py

This:
- Splits dataset into train/test

Output files:

data/processed/dft_train.pt
data/processed/dft_test.pt

----------------------------------------
4. TRAIN BVSE MODEL (PRETRAINING)
----------------------------------------

Run:

python train.py

This:
- Loads BVSE dataset
- Converts to graphs
- Trains GNN for 20 epochs

Expected output:
- Sample predictions (first epoch)
- Loss decreasing over epochs

Output file:

models/bvse_pretrained.pt

----------------------------------------
5. FINE-TUNE ON DFT DATA
----------------------------------------

Run:

python dft_finetune.py

This:
- Loads pretrained BVSE model
- Trains further on DFT dataset

Expected:
- Loss decreases slowly

Output file:

models/dft_finetuned.pt

----------------------------------------
6. TRAIN DFT MODEL FROM SCRATCH (OPTIONAL)
----------------------------------------

Run:

python DFT_Training/dft_scratch_train.py

This:
- Trains model only on DFT data

Output file:

models/dft_scratch.pt

----------------------------------------
7. EVALUATE AND COMPARE MODELS
----------------------------------------

Run:

python DFT_Training/analysis_compare.py

This:
- Evaluates scratch vs fine-tuned models
- Computes MAE and RMSE
- Generates plots

Output files:

results/metrics_comparison.csv
results/parity_comparison.png
results/error_vs_barrier.png

----------------------------------------
8. FINAL MINIMAL PIPELINE
----------------------------------------

Run all steps in order:

python inspect_data.py
python precompute_dft.py
python DFT_Training/split_dft.py
python train.py
python dft_finetune.py
python DFT_Training/analysis_compare.py

----------------------------------------
9. COMMON ERRORS
----------------------------------------

File not found:
- Check folder structure and file paths

Missing "X" atom:
- Dataset format incorrect

CUDA errors:
- Change device to CPU:
device = torch.device("cpu")

Loss not decreasing:
- Possible dataset or graph construction issue

----------------------------------------
END OF INSTRUCTIONS
----------------------------------------